## 🧠 Intuition

Two strings are called **isomorphic** if characters in one string can be replaced to get the other string while preserving the pattern.

This means:

* One character in `s` must map to **only one** character in `t`
* One character in `t` must map to **only one** character in `s`
* Mapping must be consistent throughout the string

So the relationship must be **one-to-one and two-way** (bijective).

That’s why we use **two hash maps**:

* `sTot` → maps `s[i]` to `t[i]`
* `tTos` → maps `t[i]` to `s[i]`

This prevents:

* One character mapping to multiple characters
* Multiple characters mapping to one character

No confusion. No cheating. Clean one-to-one mapping.

